      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow, a concept that's almost as mysterious as a well-hidden underground lair of goblins. But don't worry, I'll shed some light on it for you. An escrow account is essentially a holding account that holds funds until certain conditions are met, like the transfer of ownership of the house. It's like a temporary treasure chest, where your realtor's funds are kept safe until the closing process is complete.\n\nThink of it like a game of hide-and-seek with a mischievous goblin. Your realtor has to find the right moment to reveal the funds, just like how a goblin might hide a shiny coin in a tricky spot. The escrow account ensures that the funds are released only when the transaction is finalized, preventing any potential disputes or misunderstandings.\n\nIn the context of a house purchase, the escrow account typically holds funds for property taxes, insurance, and other closing costs. It's like a goblin's stash, where the funds are kept safe until the time is right to use them. Your realtor will usually set up the escrow account and manage the funds on your behalf, making sure everything runs smoothly and according to plan.\n\nNow, imagine a goblin trying to sneak into",
